re 11.2:  Children and minors who have not yet reached the age of 7 will only be permitted to travel on all national and international scheduled services if they are accompanied by an adult.
re 11.3:  Children and minors aged between 7 and 14 may only travel alone in the event that a parent or legal guardian has confirmed in writing during booking that the minor in question is both able and in a position to commence travel unaccompanied and unsupervised. Flix, FlixCompanies and their affiliates expressly do not assume any responsibility to supervise a minor. Children traveling alone may not travel on overnight services and across national borders. In addition, all children traveling alone are not authorized to participate in trips involving connections.
re 11.4:  In the case of services traveling between Greece and member states of EU, children and minors can travel independently after they have reached 6 years old. In case of accompanied children, any strollers must be put in the luggage compartment by the child’s companion.
re 16.1:  Passengers travelling between Greece and other member states may be allowed to transport small animals with the responsibility of the passenger and according to the judgement of the driver or other authorized personnel of the carrier depending on the fulness (capacity) of the vehicle and the security of the passengers (with the exception of service dogs) if:
Are put in a safe transport cage, closed type with dimensions up to 70cm x 40cm x 50cm.
They are accompanied by their owner or holder.
The owner or holder bears a personal health card – passport of the animal.
The owner or holder of the animal stays close to it and takes care for the avoidance of injury or nuisance of the other passengers.
They put the animals in free spaces of the vehicles, out of the corridors, the points of entrance/exit and ticket validation in order to not risk the safe transport of other passengers.
In case of intercity and intra-community regular and occasional service the animals must be transferred obligatory within the passenger compartment and under no circumstances in the luggage compartment (including the case of animals in parcels).
Specifically, the service dogs, namely the trained guide dogs for blind people and mobility assistance dogs for people with mobility impairments, along with dogs during the procedure of training as service dogs are transported as follows:
Without a cage and muzzle, if they have a leash, regardless their size.
The user or the trainer, as the case may be, of the service dog must bear and show, when asked by the ticket inspector or the personnel specially authorized for this purpose, the documents defined by law that certify the training sufficiency of the animal (if it is trained or under training), its health, and that the user or trainer of the dog holds the relevant certification and proof of use of the animal.
In case of a user or trainer who is a EU citizen or citizen of a third country, but stays in Greece for a short period of time, then the necessary documents, as issued by a formal agency or service from the country of origin, must be translated in the English language. In case of long term stay in Greece (i.e. reasons of work, permanent stay etc.) the aforementioned documents must be translated officially in the Greek language by the Greek Authorities abroad (Embassies etc.), according the provisions of the relevant legislation.
The user or trainer, as the case may be, of the service dog must take care of the cleanliness maintenance of the vehicle and the unobstructed transit and movement of the other passengers.
It is noted that in case of causing damage, the general provisions of the Civil Code about responsibilities of animal holder for damage inflicted by it on another person apply (Art. 924 CV).
re 14:  the carrier and their associates are under the obligation of insurance of the passengers, in the event of a road accident, during the entire length of the transport until and including the time of embarkation and disembarkation of the vehicle.
14. Additional Conditions of Carriage applicable in Albania, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Macedonia, Montenegro and Serbia
re 3.1: For journeys which start or end in Albania, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Macedonia, Montenegro and Serbia, a printed ticket is a legal requirement for carriage.
re 12.3: Bus stations have the option of charging a station service fee directly from passengers when entering the bus station.
15. Additional Conditions of Carriage applicable to Finland
re 18.4.1 and 18.6 : If luggage or other property is damaged or lost as a result of a traffic accident, the passenger is entitled to compensation in accordance with the Finnish Motor Liability Insurance Act (460/2016), and any contractual limitations on compensation set out in these provisions shall not apply. Compensation covers the actual damage to the property in accordance with applicable law. If luggage or other property is damaged or lost for any other reason, compensation shall be determined in accordance with these General Terms and Conditions of Carriage.
re 20 : Notwithstanding any jurisdiction provisions set out in these General Terms and Conditions of Carriage, if the passenger is a consumer domiciled in Finland, nothing in these General Terms and Conditions of Carriage shall limit or deprive the consumer of any mandatory rights under applicable Finnish consumer protection laws, including the right to bring proceedings before the district court (käräjäoikeus) of the consumer’s domicile. The consumer may also submit the dispute to the Finnish Consumer Disputes Board (Kuluttajariitalautakunta).
